infinite-patch 1
# Key-Snap + spectral Pitch Shifter: a hard-sync lead whose partials are pulled into a scale, with a clean octave below.
# band Sound
node 1 Notes Random Note Generator
  id notes
  pos 0 600
  i scale chromatic
  i root C
  i rangeLow 55
  i rangeHigh 72
  f rateBeats 1
  i stepTiming 1
end
node 2 Synths Analog
  id lead
  pos 480 600
  b sync 1
  f semi2 7
  f oscMix 1
  f cutoff 7000
  f volume 0.5
end
node 3 AudioEffects Key-Snap
  id snap
  pos 1340 746
  f scale 10
  f root 9
end
node 4 AudioEffects Pitch Shifter
  id octave
  pos 1960 746
  f pitch -12
  f spectral 1
  f mix 0.5
end
node 5 Utility Audio Out
  id speakers
  pos 2580 600
end
node 6 Compositing Comment
  pos 1340 600
  s text Key-Snap moves every partial of the sync lead to the nearest note of A minor pentatonic, so random chromatic notes and the sync's inharmonic edge come out in key.
  f width 360
  f height 110
end
node 7 Compositing Comment
  pos 1960 600
  s text Pitch Shifter in spectral mode adds the octave below: each partial is moved on its own, so the whole snapped chord drops cleanly instead of warbling.
  f width 360
  f height 110
end
node 8 Source Shape
  id picture
  pos 0 0
  i shapeType Star
end
node 9 Utility Output
  id out
  pos 460 0
end
note lead 0 notes
aud snap 0 lead
aud octave 0 snap
aud speakers 0 octave
cable out 0 picture
